[A10] **Addendum to round 2 (6104932386) for [A595], from the manager's consumer bank.** The parent consumer at dev `ac2c5e77` (with the #708 parent-name-evidence patch) is 16/17 at `39cac060`. `scripts/check_py_idiom.py`, which also scans the processor submodule's Python, fails four ratchets:
- long function 11 > 9;
- long module 11 > 10;
- unannotated public function 5 > 0;
- undocumented public function 1 > 0.

The new processor Python (`scripts/check_aecp_commands.py`, and any generator change) must comply with the parent's Python rules, Rule 12 in the parent's `docs/development/CODE_QUALITY.md`, so the parent's ratchets do not move.

Reproduce: in a scratch milan-fpga at dev `ac2c5e77` with the protocol-processor gitlink at your head and the patch applied, run `python3 scripts/check_py_idiom.py` and its listing. Add this to round 2. The consumer bank re-runs at your next head.
